# Runtime files Claude Code writes into its config dir. Only the settings are tracked. The
# rulebook (CLAUDE.md) and the memory live in the install (<install>/memory/talker/), linked
# in by `keel talker install`; a skill linked in here is this machine's own.
CLAUDE.md
skills/
projects/
sessions/
cache/
history.jsonl
shell-snapshots/
telemetry/
file-history/
paste-cache/
session-env/
uploads/
backups/
plugins/
.claude.json
# The login on Linux, where there is no keychain: on the box this dir is inside the
# ~/keel checkout, so without this line a credential is one `git add -A` from a commit.
.credentials.json
.claude.json.backup*
.last-cleanup
.last-update-result.json
chrome/
commands/
settings.local.json
skills/synced/
daemon/
daemon.log
jobs/
